    "en": "Ecuador is enforcing a fourth curfew through Nov. 10 in five coastal provinces as violence escalates, and the military has begun its first land operation against cartels with U.S. assistance, including U.S. Marines seizing a vessel linked to the Los Choneros gang in the eastern Pacific. Heavy rain on Santa Cruz Island in the Galapagos killed one person and left two missing, and a priest was killed when a crucifix fell on him, prompting an archbishop to announce a clergy safety plan. President Daniel Noboa continues to detain opposition leader Luisa González on money-laundering charges. The crisis recorded two battle-related deaths in 2019, according to UCDP.",
